
--- GPU memory hierarchy sweep ---
Device: Apple M4 Pro
Method: the shipped particle update body, run by a fixed grid of 262144 threads over a working set swept from 64 KiB to 16 MiB.
Every point moves the same 0 GiB, so the only variable is where the data is served from.
A plateau is one level of the hierarchy; the last one is memory.
